  "security_implications": "The kmac_done_err logic (tagged SEC_CM: KMAC_IF_DONE.CTRL.CONSISTENCY) detects unexpected KMAC done assertions outside the valid window, which could indicate an integrity attack on the handshake. The one‑hot command enables requirement prevents simultaneous adv/id/gen operations that could corrupt key material or enable unauthorized key usage. The sticky error flag without an obvious clear path may prevent recovery and maintain a fault state across transactions, potentially degrading availability or masking subsequent attacks.",
